const e="luminous-dance-competition",l=2027,n="Read both documents, each a single image-only page (Codes / Syllabus 2027 and Terms & Conditions 2027), from rendered page images. Captured: the six solo age groups, which sections run in each, the six Duo/Trio age groups and sections, the three Championships, genre definitions, all 18 General and 11 Music, Props, Venue and Awards terms, awards and judges awards. Terms 9 on both sides is split across the image halves and was read in full. Edition facts are Variables: the age date and the enquiries email (the Terms & Conditions print the email luminousdancecompetition@gmail.com). Not printed in either document: event dates, venue and address, entry fees, the price of the competitors pass, the closing date, how to submit an entry (the documents are hosted on Comps-Online but do not say so), adjudicators, marks or criteria, points per placing, minimum age, the lower age of Open Age, the age basis of duos and trios, and the Music Uploads web address. The Comps-Online contact phone number is not printed in these documents and is not copied. The adjudicator rule prints a period of 6-12 months, written as printed. The 2027 Central Coast event named in the template evidence is not named in these documents.",o={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"Luminous Dance Competition 2027. By entering any Luminous Dance Competition event you agree to follow these Terms & Conditions.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Entering",Notice:"Luminous Dance Competition is for amateurs only. Age is taken by date of birth on {{AgeDate}}. All events are non-refundable. Entries cannot be added to or changed after they close. The time limit for solos, duos and trios is 3 minutes. Questions: {{EnquiriesContact}}.",Notes:["The 2027 syllabus has two new sections: Vocal and Novice.","Music is uploaded to Music Uploads before the closing date. CDs and USBs are not accepted.","Luminous Dance Competition is a friendly and supportive place. Bullying and bad behaviour are not tolerated."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General Rules",Items:["All events run by Luminous Dance Competition are non-refundable. Credits may be given in some cases. Email {{EnquiriesContact}} for more information.","All competitors compete at their own risk. Luminous Dance Competition staff are not responsible for any injury or loss of property.","Performers are not allowed to perform with a current injury.","Luminous Dance Competition has the right to split, combine or remove sections from the event.","Luminous Dance Competition has the right to close entries before the closing date if the event sells out.","Luminous Dance Competition can run up to 1 hour early of the time given on the program. It is the competitor's duty to be there in plenty of time.","The sections run in the order of the program. If a competitor is not present, they have until the end of their section to be present. If not, they cannot perform.","Time limit for solos, duos and trios is 3 minutes. The time limit must be followed. If the music goes over the maximum of 3 minutes, there is a point deduction.","There is no special lighting, blackout or closed curtain for any act.","No rehearsals are allowed on stage during the event.","All competitors must wear stockings or tights under their costume. A competitor who is at the side of the stage without them is asked to put some on before they can perform.","Competitors have full responsibility for their props and must be able to bring them on and off stage. Props cannot be left at the venue. They must go home with the competitor.","No flames, glass, fresh fruit or flowers are allowed on stage.","The sections are Solo and Duo/Trio, in six age groups, and three Championships. The age groups and sections are in the rules of each competition.","Genre definitions: Jazz is jazz, Broadway jazz, commercial jazz and cabaret. Contemporary is expressive movement that connects the mind and body through fluid movement. Lyrical is a combination of ballet and jazz technique that tells a story through emotion and movement.","Genre definitions: Ballet is Classical Ballet, Demi Character, Neo Classical and Contemporary Ballet. Hip Hop is sharp, energetic, funky movement and can include breakdance. Tap is rhythmic sounds made by striking the floor with metal plates attached to the shoes, and all tap genres are included.","Genre definitions: Any Style is acrobatics, song and dance, musical theatre and entertainment. All Abilities is for performers living with additional needs. Vocal is for a vocal performance with no dancing. Novice is for competitors who are newer to the stage and want to build more confidence."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Eligibility",Items:["Luminous Dance Competition is for amateurs only. No professional dancers are allowed to compete.","Age is determined by date of birth and is taken on {{AgeDate}}.","It is prohibited if the competitor has been taught by, or has been associated with, the adjudicator within 6 to 12 months of the event.","A competitor must enter at least 3 solos to enter a Championship.","The age groups for solos and for duos and trios are 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age.","All competitors must buy a compulsory competitors pass for each event."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to Register",Items:["Once entries for the event have closed, you cannot add to or change your entries. Check your entries before you submit them.","Competitors must arrive at the time given on the program and wait to be signed in backstage before they go to the dressing rooms.","No CDs or USBs are accepted. Luminous Dance Competition uses Music Uploads, which needs a small fee to set up your account and a small fee to have your music uploaded for the event. All music must be uploaded to Music Uploads before the closing date."]},{Key:"fees",Title:"Fees",Items:["All events run by Luminous Dance Competition are non-refundable.","A compulsory competitors pass must be bought for each event.","Music Uploads charges a small fee to set up an account and a small fee to upload your music for the event."]},{Key:"dates",Title:"Dates and Program",Items:["Age is taken on {{AgeDate}}.","Entries can close before the closing date if the event sells out."]},{Key:"venue",Title:"Venue",Items:["No food or drink is allowed into the theatre. Only water is allowed.","No food or drink is allowed in the dressing rooms. Water is allowed.","All areas of the venue must be kept clean and left the way you found them.","Clean up after yourselves, leave the venue as you found it and tell Luminous Dance Competition staff of any issues.","No smoking is allowed inside the venue at any time."]},{Key:"levels",Title:"Rounds and Qualification",Items:["There are 3 Championship sections: Junior Championship (6 and under and 8 and under), Intermediate Championship (10 and under and 12 and under) and Senior Championship (15 and under and Open Age).","The Championship routine must be an unseen routine. This means the solo must not have been performed in the other sections on the day."]},{Key:"points",Title:"Placings",Items:["After each section, awards are presented on stage. They include the placings of each section.","If music goes over the 3 minute maximum, there is a point deduction."]},{Key:"prizes",Title:"Awards and Prizes",Items:["Solos, duos and trios: 1st, 2nd and 3rd receive a medal. Highly Commended receives a ribbon.","Championships: 1st, 2nd and 3rd receive a trophy.","Judges Awards (mini trophies): Highest Scoring in 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age; Most Entertaining Solo; Most Entertaining Duo; All Rounder; Most Promising; Encouragement Award.","Judges awards are announced on social media."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Conduct",Items:["Luminous Dance Competition is a friendly and supportive place. Bullying and bad behaviour are not tolerated.","No video or photography is allowed backstage or in the theatre. Government safety, privacy and copyright laws on the recording of sound and images apply.","By entering, you give the right for photos to be taken of the competitors on stage and behind the scenes, unless you have said otherwise.","A competitor, parent or teacher is not allowed to speak with the adjudicator at the event. This leads to a discussion with the staff of Luminous Dance Competition and may lead to disqualification."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Judging",Items:["The decisions of the adjudicators are final."]}],Documents:[{Title:"Luminous Dance Competition Codes / Syllabus 2027",Url:"https://www.comps-online.com.au/Documents/Organiser/OR000163/EV004282/Schedule/LDC_Codes_Syllabus_2027.pdf"},{Title:"Luminous Dance Competition Terms & Conditions 2027",Url:"https://www.comps-online.com.au/Documents/Organiser/OR000163/EV004282/Schedule/LDC_Terms_and_Conditions_2027.pdf"}]},t=[],a=[],i=JSON.parse('[{"Title":"Jazz","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Solo sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["Jazz is jazz, Broadway jazz, commercial jazz and cabaret."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Jazz is jazz, Broadway jazz, commercial jazz and cabaret.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"Contemporary","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Solo sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["Contemporary is expressive movement that connects the mind and body through fluid movement."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Solo section for 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age. The 6 and under group has the combined Contemporary/Lyrical section."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Contemporary is expressive movement that connects the mind and body through fluid movement.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo section for 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age. The 6 and under group has the combined Contemporary/Lyrical section."},{"Title":"Lyrical","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Solo sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["Lyrical is a combination of ballet and jazz technique that tells a story through emotion and movement."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Solo section for 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age. The 6 and under group has the combined Contemporary/Lyrical section."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Lyrical is a combination of ballet and jazz technique that tells a story through emotion and movement.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo section for 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age. The 6 and under group has the combined Contemporary/Lyrical section."},{"Title":"Contemporary/Lyrical","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Solo 6 & Under","Sections":{"About":["A combined section of the 6 and under solo group."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Solo section for 6 and under only."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A combined section of the 6 and under solo group.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo section for 6 and under only."},{"Title":"Classical Ballet, Neo Classical & Demi Character","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Solo sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["Ballet is Classical Ballet, Demi Character, Neo Classical and Contemporary Ballet."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Ballet is Classical Ballet, Demi Character, Neo Classical and Contemporary Ballet.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"Hip Hop","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Solo sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["Hip Hop is sharp, energetic, funky movement. Breakdance can be included."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Hip Hop is sharp, energetic, funky movement. Breakdance can be included.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"Any Style","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Solo sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["Any Style is acrobatics, song and dance, musical theatre and entertainment."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Any Style is acrobatics, song and dance, musical theatre and entertainment.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"Tap","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Solo sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["Tap is where performers create rhythmic sounds by striking the floor with metal plates attached to their shoes. All tap genres are included."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Tap is where performers create rhythmic sounds by striking the floor with metal plates attached to their shoes. All tap genres are included.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"All Abilities (Any Style)","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Solo sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["All Abilities is for performers living with additional needs."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- All Abilities is for performers living with additional needs.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"First Solo (Any Style)","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Solo 6 & Under and 8 & Under","Sections":{"About":["First Solo is for any style of dance. The syllabus prints it as First Solo (Anystyle)."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Solo section for 6 and under and 8 and under only."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- First Solo is for any style of dance. The syllabus prints it as First Solo (Anystyle).\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo section for 6 and under and 8 and under only."},{"Title":"Vocal","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Solo sections, Genre Definitions and New Section for 2027","Sections":{"About":["Vocal is for a vocal performance with no dancing. It is a new section for 2027."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Vocal is for a vocal performance with no dancing. It is a new section for 2027.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"Novice","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Solo sections, Genre Definitions and New Section for 2027","Sections":{"About":["Novice is for competitors who are newer to the stage and want to build more confidence. It is a new section for 2027."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Novice is for competitors who are newer to the stage and want to build more confidence. It is a new section for 2027.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"Duo/Trio Jazz","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Duo / Trio sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["Jazz is jazz, Broadway jazz, commercial jazz and cabaret."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Duo/Trio section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Jazz is jazz, Broadway jazz, commercial jazz and cabaret.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Duo/Trio section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"Duo/Trio Hip Hop","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Duo / Trio sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["Hip Hop is sharp, energetic, funky movement. Breakdance can be included."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Duo/Trio section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Hip Hop is sharp, energetic, funky movement. Breakdance can be included.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Duo/Trio section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"Duo/Trio Contemporary/Lyrical","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Duo / Trio sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["Contemporary is expressive movement that connects the mind and body through fluid movement. Lyrical is a combination of ballet and jazz technique that tells a story through emotion and movement."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Duo/Trio section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Contemporary is expressive movement that connects the mind and body through fluid movement. Lyrical is a combination of ballet and jazz technique that tells a story through emotion and movement.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Duo/Trio section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"Duo/Trio Classical Ballet, Neo Classical & Demi Character","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Duo / Trio sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["Ballet is Classical Ballet, Demi Character, Neo Classical and Contemporary Ballet."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Duo/Trio section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Ballet is Classical Ballet, Demi Character, Neo Classical and Contemporary Ballet.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Duo/Trio section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"Duo/Trio Any Style","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027, Duo / Trio sections and Genre Definitions","Sections":{"About":["Any Style is acrobatics, song and dance, musical theatre and entertainment."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Duo/Trio section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Any Style is acrobatics, song and dance, musical theatre and entertainment.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Duo/Trio section for 6 and under, 8 and under, 10 and under, 12 and under, 15 and under and Open Age."},{"Title":"Championship","Source":"LDC Codes / Syllabus 2027 and LDC Terms & Conditions 2027, Championships","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["A competitor must enter at least 3 solos to enter a Championship.","The Championship routine must be an unseen routine. This means the solo must not have been performed in the other sections on the day.","There are 3 Championship sections: Junior Championship (6 and under and 8 and under), Intermediate Championship (10 and under and 12 and under) and Senior Championship (15 and under and Open Age)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["1st, 2nd and 3rd receive a trophy."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- A competitor must enter at least 3 solos to enter a Championship.\\n- The Championship routine must be an unseen routine. This means the solo must not have been performed in the other sections on the day.\\n- There are 3 Championship sections: Junior Championship (6 and under and 8 and under), Intermediate Championship (10 and under and 12 and under) and Senior Championship (15 and under and Open Age).\\n\\n## Points\\n- 1st, 2nd and 3rd receive a trophy."}]'),s=[],d=[{Key:"AgeDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date on which age is taken",Value:"2027-01-01",Source:"LDC Terms & Conditions 2027, General 2"},{Key:"EnquiriesContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Enquiries",Value:{Name:"Luminous Dance Competition",Role:"Enquiries",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"luminousdancecompetition@gmail.com"},Source:"LDC Terms & Conditions 2027, General 3"}],r=[{Claim:"Sections, age groups, genre definitions and Championships are from the Codes / Syllabus 2027.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Luminous Dance Competition Codes / Syllabus 2027 (Comps-Online EV004282)",Url:"https://www.comps-online.com.au/Documents/Organiser/OR000163/EV004282/Schedule/LDC_Codes_Syllabus_2027.pdf"},{Claim:"General terms, music, props, venue rules, awards and Championship entry rules are from the Terms & Conditions 2027.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Luminous Dance Competition Terms & Conditions 2027 (Comps-Online EV004282)",Url:"https://www.comps-online.com.au/Documents/Organiser/OR000163/EV004282/Schedule/LDC_Terms_and_Conditions_2027.pdf"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2027,Note:n,Page:o,ParticipantTypes:t,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:d,Evidence:r};export{a as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,r as Evidence,n as Note,o as Page,t as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,d as Variables,l as Year,u as default};
